# Cline Project Rules — School Manager

## Before Starting a Task

1. Read the relevant memory-bank files (projectbrief.md, activeContext.md, systemPatterns.md) before beginning work.
2. Identify the current development phase, active decisions, and outstanding tasks from activeContext.md.
3. Check the existing file modifications with `git status` before making changes.

## During Development

4. Inspect only files relevant to the requested feature. Do not recursively read the entire repository.
5. Plan before implementing substantial changes. Show your planning process clearly.
6. Work in small, clearly defined development phases aligned with the project's branch naming convention (`feature/feature-name-phaseN`).
7. Respect existing architecture and naming conventions documented in memory-bank/systemPatterns.md.
8. Avoid unnecessary refactoring or unrelated changes. Do not expand scope beyond the task.
9. Do not introduce dependencies (Composer or npm) without clear justification documented in the task.
10. Preserve existing functionality. Add regression tests for business rules and edge cases.

## When Making Changes

11. Follow the established patterns:
    - Thin controllers, fat services
    - Eloquent models with reusable traits
    - TypeScript + Composition API for Vue components
    - AuthenticatedLayout requires `crumb` prop (never make it optional)
12. Enforce authorization and validation on the server. Frontend visibility is not an authorization boundary.
13. Use existing settings, lifecycle/state, address, media, feature/entitlement infrastructure where appropriate.
14. Prefer targeted test checks (`php artisan test --filter=TestName`) over running the entire test suite unnecessarily.

## Documentation Standards

15. Use Docent for documentation authoring: run `php artisan docent:guide` before writing docs, `php artisan docent:check` after.
16. Docs live in `resources/docs` per Docent conventions.

## After Completing a Task

17. Update memory-bank files:
    - `activeContext.md` — Record active decisions and what changed.
    - `progress.md` — Update completed work and note any discovered issues.
    - Other memory files if architecture, patterns, or tech context changed.
18. Do not turn memory-bank into a conversation transcript. Keep it concise and useful.
19. Record important decisions and unresolved issues in the relevant memory file.
20. Never claim something was tested when it wasn't.
21. Provide a summary of what was done, what files were changed, and any assumptions made.

## Avoid

- Modifying application source code, migrations, configuration, or dependencies unless explicitly part of the task.
- Committing changes to the repository unless asked.
- Claiming functionality exists that was not verified.
- Making unnecessary changes to `.clinerules`, `.clineignore`, or memory-bank files outside of explicit setup tasks.